atient will follow up in 2 months. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nYearly exam.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nBeverly is a 24-year-old female who presents for a yearly exam. She has a history of type 2 diabetes and hypertension. She has been doing well, but she started working in a bakery this summer and finds herself snacking a lot during shifts and eating a lot more desserts than she normally would.\n\nThe patient reports that her blood sugars have been up and down. She states she has been taking her Metformin as prescribed, but her diet has been pretty bad lately. She denies missing any doses of Metformin.\n\nThe patient reports that her blood pressure has been good. She states she has been sleeping well, getting a full 8 hours per night. She denies any suicidal ideation.\n\nThe patient states that she has been checking her blood sugars. She denies any chest pain, shortness of breath, or any other symptoms.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Denies fever, chills, or fatigue. Denies weight loss.\nCardiovascular: Denies chest pain, dyspnea on exertion, or syncope.\nEndocrine: Denies polyuria, polydipsia, or other symptoms of diabetes.\nNeurological: Denies focal weakness, focal numbness, or focal tingling.\nPsychiatric: Denies depression, anxiety, or suicidal ideation.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\nConstitutional: In no acute distress.\nSkin: No rashes, lesions, or lesions.\nNeurological: Cranial nerves grossly intact. Strength and reflexes equal and symmetric.\nCardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm. Grade 2/6 systolic ejection murmur.\nRespiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.\nMusculoskeletal: No edema in the extremities. No clubbing.\nNeurological: No carotid bruits. No thyromegaly. Pulses are equal and strong.\n\nRESULTS\n\nHemoglobin A1c: Elevated.\n\nVITALS\n\nBlood pressure: 130/80 mmHg.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nBeverly is a 24-year-old female with a past medical history significant for type 2 diabetes and hypert