atient will follow up in 2 months. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nAnnual gynecological exam.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nBev erly is a 24-year-old female who presents today for her annual gynecological exam. She has a history of type 2 diabetes and hypertension. She reports that her diabetes has been out of control due to her diet. She states that she is currently working at a bakery and she is having a hard time resisting the temptation of baked goods. She reports that she has been taking her medication as prescribed. She states that her blood pressure has been good and that she has been sleeping well and denies any headaches or dizziness. She denies any joint pain, muscle aches, or numbness and tingling. She states that she has been urinating more frequently. She denies any chest pain or palpitations. She denies any shortness of breath, cough, wheezing, or sneezing. She denies any nasal congestion or sinus pain. She denies any ear pain or discharge. She denies any sore throat. She denies any hoarseness. She denies any nasal congestion, sinus pain, or discharge. She denies any ear pain or discharge. She denies any throat pain. She denies any headaches or dizziness. She denies any joint pain, muscle aches, or numbness and tingling. She denies any nausea or vomiting. She denies any diarrhea or constipation. She denies any chest pain or palpitations. She denies any shortness of breath, cough, wheezing, or sneezing. She denies any nasal congestion or sinus pain. She denies any ear pain or discharge. She denies any sore throat. She denies any headaches or dizziness. She denies any joint pain, muscle aches, or numbness and tingling. She denies any nausea or vomiting. She denies any diarrhea or constipation. She denies any chest pain or palpitations. She denies any shortness of breath, cough, wheezing, or sneezing. She denies any nasal congestion or sinus pain. She denies any ear pain or discharge. She denies any throat pain. She denies any hea