s any muscle aches. He reports that he has been exercising, but he does not feel confident in his exercise routine. He is also concerned about the use of NSAIDs. He denies any issues with his kidney function.\n\nThe patient is a former resident of the West Coast. He is a San Francisco 49ers fan. He is excited about the Super Bowl.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Denies fever, chills, or weight loss.\nCardiovascular: Denies chest pain, dyspnea on exertion.\nRespiratory: Denies shortness of breath.\nGastrointestinal: Denies nausea or vomiting.\nGenitourinary: Denies hematuria or dysuria.\nMusculoskeletal: Denies muscle aches.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\nNeck\n- General Examination: No jugular venous distention. No carotid bruits.\n- Heart\n- Auscultation of Heart: Slight 3/6 systolic ejection murmur heard at the left base.\n- Lower Extremities\n- Examination: 1+ pitting edema in the lower extremities.\n\nRESULTS\n\nKidney function was stable.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\n1. Coronary artery disease.\n- Medical Reasoning: The patient is doing well and is compliant with his medications. We will refer him to cardiac rehab for exercise tolerance improvement.\n- Medical Treatment: Continue metoprolol 50 mg once daily and Crestor 40 mg once daily.\n\n2. Chronic kidney disease, stage 3.\n- Medical Reasoning: His kidney function is stable.\n- Medical Treatment: We will refer him to Dr. Miller for follow-up.\n\n3. Diabetes.\n- Medical Reasoning: His last hemoglobin A1c was 60.\n- Medical Treatment: We will order another hemoglobin A1c. We will refer him to a dietitian for education and we will contact his primary care physician about his insulin regimen.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nThe patient will follow up with Dr. Miller for his kidney disease. He will follow up with a dietitian for education on his diabetes. He will continue his current medications. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response 