 mg daily. We will repeat another echo in about 2 months. Her third diagnosis is hypertension. Her blood pressure is fine, and she is tolerating her medications. We will add Aldactone 12.5 mg daily. We will consider nutrition counseling for diet modifications. She will repeat her labs. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nAcute onset chest pain.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY\n\nPatient reports she has been walking her dog daily, approximately 1.5 to 2 miles. She is looking forward to the holiday season and has plans to see family.\n\nMEDICATIONS\n\n• Aspirin 81 mg daily\n• Brilinta 90 mg twice daily\n• Lipitor 80 mg daily\n• Toprol 50 mg daily\n• Metformin\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Cardiovascular: Reports chest pain. Denies dyspnea.\n• Respiratory: Denies dyspnea.\n• Musculoskeletal: Reports leg edema. Denies back pain.\n• Neurological: Denies headaches, weakness, and numbness.\n• Skin: Denies rashes, itching, and skin lesions.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\n• Neck: No jugular venous distension. No carotid bruits.\n• Cardiovascular: Grade 3/6 systolic ejection murmur at the left base. Regular rate and rhythm. No extra heart sounds. No gallops.\n• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n• Musculoskeletal: 1+ pitting edema of the right leg.\n\nRESULTS\n\nEKG: Normal sinus rhythm. Good R wave progression. Evolutionary changes anticipated after a STEMI.\n\nRESULTS\n\nECHO: Reduced ejection fraction of 35%. Moderate mitral regurgitation.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\n1. Coronary artery disease.\n• Medical Reasoning: Patient has a history of coronary artery disease.\n• Patient Education and Counseling: Continue aspirin 81 mg daily and Brilinta 90 mg twice daily. Continue high-dose statin Lipitor 80 mg daily. Continue Toprol 50 mg daily.\n2. Reduced left ventricular dysfunction and moderate mitral regurgitation.\n• Medical Reasoning: Patient has reduced left ventricular dysfunction and moderate mitral regurgitation.\n• Patient Education and Counseling: Continue Li